    "durationMs": 168767,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation** (Rails 8.0.2 API-only, PostgreSQL via Active Record):\n- `app/models/link.rb` — validates `url` as an absolute http/https URI with a host, `code` against `/\\A[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{4,20}\\z/` with uniqueness, and auto-generates a 6-char code when omitted.\n- `app/controllers/links_controller.rb` — `POST /links` (201/409/422), `GET /links` (ascending order + total), `GET /links/:code` (200/404), `GET /r/:code` (302 with `redirect_to`, atomic `increment_counter` so clicks go up exactly once per request).\n- `app/controllers/application_controller.rb` — rescues malformed JSON as 422.\n- `db/migrate/..._create_links.rb` — `links` table with non-null `url`, unique-indexed `code`, `clicks` defaulting to 0.\n- `config/environments/production.rb` — disabled `force_ssl`/`assume_ssl` so plain-HTTP requests on port 8000 aren't redirected.\n- `start.sh` — runs `db:prepare` (migrations) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; reads DB settings from `DATABASE_URL`, generates a `SECRET_KEY_BASE` if absent, installs nothing.\n- `README.md` — documents how to start the server and the endpoints.\n\n**Verified with curl**: generated and custom codes (including 4/20-char boundaries), duplicate → 409, invalid URLs (`ftp://`, no host, `javascript:`, missing/blank) → 422, invalid codes → 422, malformed JSON → 422, 302 redirect with correct `Location`, click counts 1→2→3 across redirects, unknown codes → 404 with `error`, and full data + click-count persistence across a server restart. Test server was stopped afterward."
  }
